    "ref": "PR #1403 (fix); fix evidence: Plan #1403 item 11 (code read 16/10/2026): a follow-up a broken release or a disposal cancelled — one the model never saw — ended as a notice asking the customer to send it again; cut-by-deploy.json, written by deploy-host-dsh.sh since #295, had no reader, so every interrupted turn was blamed on an update, a crash or a host reboot included",
    "invariant": "S1: the cancelled message is put back at the head of the queue (state held, resent: true in the file), released by the next pass, and the model is asked 'one' then 'two' — each once; nothing left to tell. S2: sent once more, then a failed notice for it; released exactly twice; the model never asked. S3: true only for cancelled or claimed messages, once, while nothing newer was written; false otherwise. S4: cutAt lists that deploy's time for the conversation's own site, [] for another site; the plain answer carries no cutAt. S5: \"This request was interrupted by a Tracy update.\" for the first; \"This request was interrupted when Tracy restarted.\" for every other, never \"Tracy update\".",
